# Struct Tabs Copy item path

[Source](https://docs.rs/ratatui-widgets/0.3.2/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/src/ratatui_widgets/tabs.rs.html#51)

```
pub struct Tabs<'a> { /* private fields */ }
```

Expand description

A widget that displays a horizontal set of Tabs with a single tab selected.

Each tab title is stored as a [`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line") which can be individually styled. The selected tab is set using [`Tabs::select`](struct.Tabs.html#method.select "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::select") and styled using [`Tabs::highlight_style`](struct.Tabs.html#method.highlight_style "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::highlight_style"). The divider can be customized with [`Tabs::divider`](struct.Tabs.html#method.divider "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::divider"). Padding can be set with [`Tabs::padding`](struct.Tabs.html#method.padding "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::padding") or [`Tabs::padding_left`](struct.Tabs.html#method.padding_left "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::padding_left") and [`Tabs::padding_right`](struct.Tabs.html#method.padding_right "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::padding_right").

The divider defaults to |, and padding defaults to a singular space on each side.

## [§](#example)Example

```
use ratatui::style::{Style, Stylize};
use ratatui::symbols;
use ratatui::widgets::{Block, Tabs};

Tabs::new(vec!["Tab1", "Tab2", "Tab3", "Tab4"])
    .block(Block::bordered().title("Tabs"))
    .style(Style::default().white())
    .highlight_style(Style::default().yellow())
    .select(2)
    .divider(symbols::DOT)
    .padding("->", "<-");
```

In addition to `Tabs::new`, any iterator whose element is convertible to `Line` can be collected into `Tabs`.

```
use ratatui::widgets::Tabs;

(0..5).map(|i| format!("Tab{i}")).collect::<Tabs>();
```

