#### pub fn [new](#method.new)<Iter>(titles: Iter) -> [Tabs](struct.Tabs.html "struct ratatui::widgets::Tabs")<'a>

where Iter: [IntoIterator](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/collect/trait.IntoIterator.html "trait core::iter::traits::collect::IntoIterator"), <Iter as [IntoIterator](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/collect/trait.IntoIterator.html "trait core::iter::traits::collect::IntoIterator")\>::[Item](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/iter/traits/collect/trait.IntoIterator.html#associatedtype.Item "type core::iter::traits::collect::IntoIterator::Item"): [Into](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")<[Line](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line")<'a>>,

Creates new `Tabs` from their titles.

`titles` can be a [`Vec`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html "struct alloc::vec::Vec") of [`&str`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/primitive.str.html "primitive str"), [`String`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/string/struct.String.html "struct alloc::string::String") or anything that can be converted into [`Line`](../prelude/struct.Line.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Line"). As such, titles can be styled independently.

The selected tab can be set with [`Tabs::select`](struct.Tabs.html#method.select "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::select"). The first tab has index 0 (this is also the default index).

The selected tab can have a different style with [`Tabs::highlight_style`](struct.Tabs.html#method.highlight_style "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::highlight_style"). This defaults to a style with the [`Modifier::REVERSED`](../prelude/struct.Modifier.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Modifier") modifier added.

The default divider is a pipe (`|`), but it can be customized with [`Tabs::divider`](struct.Tabs.html#method.divider "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::divider").

The entire widget can be styled with [`Tabs::style`](struct.Tabs.html#method.style "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::style").

The widget can be wrapped in a [`Block`](struct.Block.html "struct ratatui::widgets::Block") using [`Tabs::block`](struct.Tabs.html#method.block "method ratatui::widgets::Tabs::block").

